\f1\b Profit
\f0\b0  
\f1\b on
\f0\b0  
\f1\b a
\f0\b0  
\f1\b win:
\f0\b0 \
  - Positive odds (+150): \cf3 profit\cf2  \cf3 =\cf2  \cf3 wager\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 (odds\cf2  \cf3 /\cf2  \cf3 100)\cf2  \uc0\u8594  $10 at +150 wins $15\
  - Negative odds (-110): \cf3 profit\cf2  \cf3 =\cf2  \cf3 wager\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 (100\cf2  \cf3 /\cf2  \cf3 |odds|)\cf2  \uc0\u8594  $11 at -110 wins $10\
  - Total return = wager + profit\
\
  
\f1\b Boost:
\f0\b0  Some books offer odds boosts. A boost lifts the odds by that percentage of itself \'97 in a favorable\
  direction regardless of sign.\
  - \cf3 +200\cf2  with 20% boost \uc0\u8594  \cf3 +200\cf2  \cf3 +\cf2  \cf3 (200\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 0.20)\cf2  = 
\f1\b +240
\f0\b0 \
  - \cf3 -110\cf2  with 20% boost \uc0\u8594  \cf3 -110\cf2  \cf3 +\cf2  \cf3 (110\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 0.20)\cf2  = 
\f1\b -88
\f0\b0  (closer to even, i.e. better)\
\
  All P&L calculations use the 
\f1\b boosted
\f0\b0  
\f1\b odds
\f0\b0 , not the base odds. Base odds are just stored for reference.\
\
