\f1\b 2.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Wager
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Splits
\f0\b0 \
\
  Each bet has three wager fields:\
  - \cf3 total_wager\cf2  \'97 total staked by the pool\
  - \cf3 his_wager\cf2  (Dan) \'97 Dan's share\
  - \cf3 my_wager\cf2  (Brent) \'97 Brent's share\
\
  They must always sum: \cf3 his_wager\cf2  \cf3 +\cf2  \cf3 my_wager\cf2  \cf3 =\cf2  \cf3 total_wager\cf2 \
\
  
\f1\b When
\f0\b0  
\f1\b a
\f0\b0  
\f1\b bet
\f0\b0  
\f1\b wins
\f0\b0 , each person's return is proportional to their share:\
  person_return = total_return \'d7 (person_wager / total_wager)\
  person_profit = person_return \uc0\u8722  person_wager\
\
  Example: $50 total bet at +200 (returns $150). Dan put in $35, Brent $15.\
  - Dan's return: \cf3 $150\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 (35/50)\cf2  = 
\f1\b $105
\f0\b0  \uc0\u8594  profit of 
\f1\b +$70
\f0\b0 \
  - Brent's return: \cf3 $150\cf2  \cf3 \'d7\cf2  \cf3 (15/50)\cf2  = 
\f1\b $45
\f0\b0  \uc0\u8594  profit of 
\f1\b +$30
\f0\b0 \
\
