\f1\b 3.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b The
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Pool
\f0\b0 \
\
  
\f1\b Total
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Pool
\f0\b0  = sum of all sportsbook balances + bucket\
\
  
\f1\b Bucket
\f0\b0  = money withdrawn from sportsbooks but not yet paid out to either person. It accumulates when you log a\
   withdrawal and drains when you log a payout/disbursement.\
\
  ---\
  
\f1\b 4.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Dan's
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Equity
\f0\b0 \
\
  Dan's equity is calculated 
\f1\b explicitly
\f0\b0  from the ground up:\
\
  Dan's equity = his deposits\
               \uc0\u8722  payouts he's received\
               + profit on every won bet (his share)\
               \uc0\u8722  wager on every lost bet (his share)\
               \uc0\u8722  wager on every pending bet (treated as a loss)\
\
  Pending bets count as losses in real-time. This gives you a "live" conservative number \'97 equity only goes up\
  when bets actually win.\
\
  ---\
  
\f1\b 5.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Brent's
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Equity
\f0\b0 \
\
  Brent's equity is 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  calculated the same way as Dan's. Instead it's a 
\f1\b residual
\f0\b0 :\
\
  Brent's equity = Total Pool \uc0\u8722  Dan's equity\
\
  This is intentional and mathematically correct. Because the pool holds all the money, the two equities must\
  always sum to the total. Brent absorbs everything the explicit Dan calculation doesn't account for \'97 including\
   any solo bets Brent placed where \cf3 his_wager\cf2  \cf3 =\cf2  \cf3 $0\cf2 , and any rounding or adjustments.\
\
  ---\
  
\f1\b 6.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Pending
\f0\b0  
\f1\b =
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Live
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Loss
\f0\b0 \
\
  Both Dan's equity and per-person P&L stats treat open/pending bets as if they already lost. This means:\
\
  - Equity shows your 
\f1\b floor
\f0\b0  \'97 the worst-case number if every open bet loses\
  - When a pending bet wins, equity jumps up by the full profit\
  - When it loses (as expected), nothing changes \'97 it was already priced in\
\
